TzD (task #42): mab_mas_cp() writes pivots only inside pivots[].
For a full node the copy loop writes pivots[mt_pivots[mt]], one past the
pivot array: it lands on slots[0] of the same node, which the memcpy
right after overwrites, so the store has no effect.  TzD bounds &pivot
to the array and traps (kdevtmpfs).  Skip the store past the array.
--- a/lib/maple_tree.c	2026-11-13 19:14:02.696690659 +0900
+++ b/lib/maple_tree.c	2026-11-13 19:14:02.722193868 +0900
@@ -1995,7 +1995,13 @@
 
 	i = mab_start;
 	do {
-		pivots[j++] = b_node->pivot[i++];
+		/* A node has one pivot fewer than slots: the last slot's is
+		   the node's maximum.  pivots[mt_pivots[mt]] would land on
+		   slots[0], which the memcpy below writes anyway.  */
+		if (j < mt_pivots[mt])
+			pivots[j] = b_node->pivot[i];
+		j++;
+		i++;
 	} while (i <= mab_end && likely(b_node->pivot[i]));
 
 	memcpy(slots, b_node->slot + mab_start,
